WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.369
-The president gave a speech
on Saturday

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.905
about the government shutdown
and offered an immigration deal

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.773
that both Democrats
and hard-line conservatives

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:08.975
have rejected.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.210
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.346
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.316
President Trump's speech
on Saturday

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:20.086
was mostly just a collection of
the same debunked talking points

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.387
he's been repeating for weeks.

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.622
And as usual,
he spent the whole time

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:27.126
sucking in air like
he was running a marathon.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.627
Here are some highlights.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.563
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.432
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.773
-Good Lord!

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:43.075
That sounded like
the first 20 minutes

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.178
of a movie about Pablo Escobar.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.746
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.214
Maybe Trump is laboring

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.050
because he knows every time
he gives one of these speeches,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.152
it gets harder and harder
to convince people.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.688
On Saturday, for example,
he floated a new proposal.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.691
In exchange for wall money, he
would offer temporary extensions

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.293
for recipients of two programs
that protect immigrants

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.129
known as DACA and TPS.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.130
And not only
did Democrats reject it,

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.166
but so did
hard-line conservatives.

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:09.269
Right-wing pundit Ann Coulter
tweeted,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:13.038
"Trump proposes amnesty.
We voted for Trump and got Jeb."

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.540
Wow.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.611
She compared him to Jeb Bush,
his nemesis from the primaries.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.647
Trump prides himself
on being a master negotiator.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.049
Here is actual footage

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:26.652
of Jeb Bush's
most successful negotiation.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:27.820
-Please clap.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.755
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.557
-But, of course, the guy's --

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.993
The comparison is unfair.
It's ridiculous.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.829
I mean, it's not like Trump
has ever asked a crowd

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.564
to give him a standing ovation.

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:39.698
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:40.833
-Get up.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.335
-Oh, my God.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.337
It's happening!
He's turning into Jeb.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.472
Soon he's going to start
wearing glasses

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.474
and getting trapped
in his own hoodie.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:49.642
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.277
Even Trump's speeches
are low-energy now.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.879
When he runs for re-election
in 2020,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.114
the primary debates are just
going to be a split screen

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.283
of him making faces at himself.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.884
-That is our plan.

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:04.591
Border security, DACA, TPS,
and many other things.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.026
-Now, we are living
in a very surreal time

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.661
where people like Ann Coulter

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.029
have tremendous sway
over the president.

00:02:11.029 --> 00:02:13.399
In December, Trump was going to
give up on the wall

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.101
until Coulter
called him a gutless

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.436
and a vulgar publicity hound.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.470
He then went to try
to win her back.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.906
Trump shut down the government.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.941
And once again,
after Coulter insulted him

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.242
and called the deal amnesty,

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.444
Trump scrambled to make
her happy by tweeting,

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:28.715
"No, amnesty is not
a part of my offer."

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.950
Man, why is he
so subservient to her?

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.086
Does she have
a different pee tape?

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.388
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.458
Here's the thing.
Trump's proposal is not amnesty.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.392
It's not even a reasonable deal.

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.327
And there's no reason to believe
he'll follow through on it.

00:02:42.327 --> 00:02:44.563
Remember, we've been down
this road many times with him.

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:46.632
And every time,
he's reneged on his promises.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:49.335
As early as February 2017,

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.769
he said he wanted
to protect DREAMers,

00:02:50.769 --> 00:02:52.104
the young
undocumented immigrants

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:53.105
brought here as children,

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.907
and that he would be open
to a bill

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.075
that would give them
permanent legal status.

00:02:57.075 --> 00:03:00.713
-On the DACA program for
immigration, what is your plan?

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.515
Do you plan to continue
that program or to end it?

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:05.051
-We're going to
show great heart.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.955
DACA is a very, very difficult
subject for me, I will tell you.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.457
To me, it's one of the most
difficult subjects I have,

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.393
because you have
these incredible kids.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.328
We are going to deal with DACA
with heart.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.198
The DACA situation
is a very, very --

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.934
It's a very difficult thing
for me.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.102
Because, you know,
I love these kids.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.604
I love kids.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:25.738
I have kids.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.407
-"I have kids!

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.574
I have kids.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.476
I've only ever tried
to deport two of them.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.711
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:35.081
Sorry, boys.
Back to Transylvania."

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.715
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:38.084
That was in February 2017.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.286
In September,
Trump canceled the program.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.454
Then in January,

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.656
he told lawmakers
he was open to a compromise.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.157
And then two days after that,

00:03:45.157 --> 00:03:47.026
he completely
changed his mind again.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:49.062
And even Republican senator
Lindsey Graham,

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.496
who brokered the compromise

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.898
and has become one of Trump's
closest allies in Congress,

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.401
was stunned by Trump's
sudden change of heart.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:04:00.606
-Tuesday we had a president
that I was proud to golf with,

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:01.874
call my friend,

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.111
who understood immigration
had to be bipartisan.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.513
You had to have border security.
It's essential.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.782
You have border security
with the wall,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.484
but he also understood the idea

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.652
that we had to do it
with compassion.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:16.656
Now, I don't know
where that guy went.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.323
I want him back.

00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:21.961
-Oh! Why did he suddenly
change his mind out of nowhere?

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.764
Because he's President Werewolf!

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.766
Except he's a werewolf
29 days a month

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.201
and then there's a full moon,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.603
he turns into a human,
and you can talk to him.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.037
And then all you dummies
celebrate

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.406
because you think
it's permanent.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:34.707
Then the full moon goes away,

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.476
and he goes back to chasing you
through the woods.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.444
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.880
You can't negotiate with someone
who doesn't know anything,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.214
who changes his mind constantly,

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.517
and who lives in fear of
Ann Coulter's Twitter account.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.718
There's really only one person

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.253
who can end this shutdown
right now,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.255
and that's Senate Majority
Leader Mitch McConnell.

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.423
The Senate has already passed a
bill to keep the government open

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:52.758
with no strings attached.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:54.994
All McConnell has to do
is pass that same bill again

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.595
and override
the president's veto,

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.564
and the government
would open up immediately,

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.134
which is why a group
of freshmen Democrats,

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:02.968
led by Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.637
showed up in his office
last week

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.438
demanding to know
what he was doing.

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:09.508
-We have voted repeatedly,
over and over again,

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.177
to reopen the government.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.645
We went to his office
in the Capitol.

00:05:13.645 --> 00:05:15.647
We went to his office
here in the Russell Building.

00:05:15.647 --> 00:05:17.249
We went to the floor.
-To the cloakroom.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:19.318
-We went to the cloakroom.
He's not in the cloakroom.

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.352
He's not in the Capitol.

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:21.721
He's not in
the Russell Building.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.255
He's not in the floor
of the Senate,

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.457
and 800,000 people
don't have their paychecks.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:27.026
So where's Mitch?

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.728
-I mean -- Yeah.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:36.569
Although I will say, if you're
ever wondering where's Mitch,

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.871
just go down to the marsh
and check the lily pads.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.373
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.373 --> 00:05:43.309
We've been down this road
with Trump before.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:44.877
And there's no reason
to trust him

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.445
any more than we have
in the past.

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:47.779
The Senate could pass a bill
right now

00:05:47.779 --> 00:05:49.181
to reopen the government.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.751
In the meantime, millions of
people are needlessly suffering,

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.986
and all the president
has to say to them is...

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.088
-[ Breathing heavily ]

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:57.823
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:05:57.823 --> 00:06:00.026
[ Cheers and applause ]

